My Inventory control system
The aim of this presentation is to inform the audience of my inventory control system. 
It will cover the instructions, setup, design and steps taken to finalize the inventory control  system.

Designing the system
Requirements gathering. This is where I define the system’s objective and functional requirements
The system will need to tract  down the ownership details and transaction history
Choosing the right programming language for my system is crucial hence that is why I’ve opted to use python as my programming language.
Lastly the system should include a user interface.

Database design
It will contain the ownership details and gun information.
It will have data normalization so that it should reduce redundancy of items or requests.
The database will also need to be secure for protecting our customers information. 

User interface design
This will contain the different roles of users for example some users can be law enforcements or just regular people purchase a gun for safety.
Testing will be conducted to make room for improvement.

Security
Security measures will be implemented to protect sensitive data for example encryption.
The system will also comply  with regular regulations for firearms so that the only people buying a gun should be responsible for it.
Regular testing will be taking place before the system is deployed so that it can be effective with zero errors. 

Testing 
The system will be integrating with relevant systems for compatibility.
The system should address any bugs and faults that may arise to ensure effectiveness.

Deployment 
The system will eventually be deployed in a secure and controlled environment.
Monitoring will take place to see how the system is performing and address any issues that have risen.

Maintenance and updates
The should will be regularly updated to ensure that there are no errors rising.
User feedback will be monitored to meet user needs hence competitive advantage.

Debugging
The system should be able to perform debugging on it’s own with minimal efforts.
Debugging should be very fast and accurate to make it convenient.

